Goal: Finalize and validate the existing uncommitted work in this repository: fixes for DOG-040, DOG-041, DOG-042 and DOG-043 (see their entries at the end of dogfood/findings/FINDINGS.md, the change_log.md entries, and documentation/ORCHESTRATE.md).

- DOG-042: an implementation attempt whose output declares IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS: INCOMPLETE is recorded as IMPLEMENTATION_INCOMPLETE (not success), keeps partial changes and the stated reason, and the next implementer continues; the session hands off when none can.
- DOG-041: when an explicit --verify differs from the plan's VERIFY_COMMAND, review and acceptance are told which command verifies the session.
- DOG-043: user-correctable orchestrate refusals raise OrchestrateRequestError and render as ORCHESTRATE_REQUEST_REFUSED with a next step instead of INTERNAL_ERROR; internal failures keep their handling.
- DOG-040: a refusal of only named Bash commands in a mutating role is a session-scoped grant gap whether or not files changed; edit-tool refusals and unnamed denials still mark the agent interactive-only. One existing DOG-018 test was intentionally revised.

If the existing change is correct and complete, report IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS: NO_CHANGE_REQUIRED with reasons; otherwise fix only what is wrong and add tests. HowlPlane runs `make test-full` itself and supplies the result; run only targeted tests. Reviewers: try to falsify each fix, including: prose that merely mentions INCOMPLETE; INCOMPLETE during rework rounds and its effect on rework counting; whether IMPLEMENTATION_INCOMPLETE could be abused to dodge review; refusals still raised as plain ValueError that a user can correct; any real HowlPlane bug now hidden as a user error; whether DOG-040 lets an agent that truly cannot edit unattended stay marked ready in a way that would repeatedly waste sessions; and documentation claims the code does not keep.
